We now outline our approach to construct a nonzero map between supernatural sheaves on $\mathbb{P}^s$ of types $f\preceq f'$ in the case that $\ell(f) = \ell(f') = s$. 
This uses the proof of~\cite{EiScConjOfBS07}*{Theorem~6.1}. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Construct a finite map $\pi\colon  \mathbb{P}^{1\times s}\to \mathbb{P}^{s}$.
\item Choose appropriate line bundles $\mathcal L$ and $\mathcal L'$ on $\mathbb{P}^{1\times s}$ 
	so that $\pi_* \mathcal L$ and $\pi_*\mathcal L'$ are supernatural vector bundles
	of the desired types.
\item When $\ell(f) = \ell(f') = s$, construct a morphism $\mathcal L' \stackrel{\phi}{\longrightarrow}
    \mathcal L$ such that $\pi_* \phi$ is nonzero.
\end{enumerate}

By~\cite{fulton}*{\S9.4}, the existence of such a $\mu$ is
equivalent to the condition
\begin{equation} \lambda''_i + \lambda^c_{n-i} \le  \lambda_1+N_1 \quad \text{for }
  i=1,\dots,n-1.
\end{equation}

Let 
\begin{equation} r :=\max\{d_{\ell(d)}-d_0-\ell(d), d'_{\ell(d')}-d_0-\ell(d')\}
\end{equation}
and $\mathbb{P} := \mathbb{P}^{n-1}\times \mathbb{P}^{1\times r}$.
